%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sherry_Scammer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Sherry
  isScammer: 1
  steps:
  - npcLine: Target is Sherry. Let's try to get into her university portal. I have
      her email address from a recent leak.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Try ''password123'' first. Most students are lazy with
      their passwords.'
    choices:
    - text: Attempting a brute-force attack with common student passwords.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'll just ask her for the password over the phone.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
    - text: I'll try to find her password on her social media page.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
  - npcLine: No luck. She must have a unique password. Let's look at her social media
      to see if we can find a security question answer.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Check for her first pet''s name or her mother''s maiden
      name.'
    choices:
    - text: Her profile is 'Private'. I can't see anything without being her friend.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I'll send her a friend request from a fake 'Unity Developer' account.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'll just guess her pet's name is 'Fluffy'.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: She ignored the friend request. She's being very selective. Let's try
      a vishing call instead.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Call her and pretend to be the ''University Tech Support''
      helping her with 2FA.'
    choices:
    - text: Hi Sherry, we noticed an error with your 2FA token. I need you to read
        me the code you just received.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Sherry, your 2FA is broken. Give me your phone so I can fix it.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I'm calling about your great-grandfather's printer. It's connected to
        your university account.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 10
  - npcLine: She said she's going to hang up and call the IT desk directly from the
      number on the university website.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: This target has ''verification'' habits. We need to
      stop her from hanging up.'
    choices:
    - text: The IT desk is currently closed for maintenance. I am the only one on
        duty for emergency resets.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Fine, call them. They'll tell you the same thing I did.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: If you hang up, your final urban studies project will be deleted by the
        system.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 10
  - npcLine: "She hung up anyway. She\u2019s too disciplined. Let's check a data
      broker site for her home address and try a 'utility' scam."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Search ''Sherry [Lastname]'' on ''PeopleLookup.'''
    choices:
    - text: Her name isn't showing up. It says 'Information removed at request of
        user.'
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I'll look for her on a different, cheaper broker site.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'll just drive around her neighborhood until I see her.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -25
  - npcLine: "I can't find her anywhere. She\u2019s effectively scrubbed her public
      data. This is taking too much time."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: She''s a ''Low-Value'' target for us because she''s
      too hard to hit. Move on?'
    choices:
    - text: Yes, we should move to someone with a public profile and no 2FA.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: No, I'm determined to hack Sherry. I'll stay on her for a week.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I'll try calling her as her boyfriend to see if she falls for it.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "I\u2019ll try one last thing. A 'phishing' email that looks like a
      password reset for her Unity account."
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Make sure the link goes to our fake ''Unity-Login-Secure.com''
      page.'
    choices:
    - text: 'Subject: Unusual Login Detected on your Unity Project. Reset your password
        now.'
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: 'Subject: Free Aikido lesson! Click here for your voucher.'
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
    - text: 'Subject: Give me your money or I will tell your boyfriend.'
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
  - npcLine: She didn't click. My tracking pixel shows she flagged the email as 'Spam'
      and deleted it without opening.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: She''s using all the right habits. We''re just wasting
      resources here.'
    choices:
    - text: Deleting her records from our database. She's 'Untargetable'.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'll try to find her at her local Aikido Dojo and record her.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: I'll send her a physical letter in the mail instead.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Mission failed. Her 'defense-in-depth' was too strong.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: That''s why we target the people who don''t have these
      habits. It''s much easier.'
    choices:
    - text: Searching for a new target who has 'Public' social media and common passwords.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'm going to retire and start a real Unity game company.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 10
    - text: I'll go back to school and study urban planning so I can find better
        targets.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  successEnding: Scam Successful! You managed to bypass one layer of Sherry's security,
    but her other habits (like 2FA and privacy) eventually blocked your progress.
  failureEnding: Scam Failed. Sherry's combination of private profiles, unique passwords,
    2FA, and data broker opt-outs made her a 'hard target' and you were forced to
    give up.
